      "message": "ci(post-merge): one independent run per merge\n\nEach push to main gets its own concurrency group\n(post-merge-${{ inputs.ref || github.sha }}, cancel-in-progress: false).\nNo run waits behind another run, and no run is cancelled. A red run\nnames exactly its own commit.\n\nRuns can finish out of order. The report job runs one at a time\n(group post-merge-report) with the full history. The report script\nkeeps the last reported commit in a hidden marker in the rolling issue\nbody and skips a run whose commit is a strict ancestor of it.\n\nPinned by xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs and the order tests in\nxtask/tests/post_merge_report.rs (real git history, fake gh).\n\nFixes #3184\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
